    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d174">

                <pb facs="0509" n="395" xml:id="pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to
                        Prime Minister Churchill
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d174-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-07-21">July 21, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 320 personal and secret from the President for the Former Naval Person.</p>
                <p>Referring to your numbers 371 and 372,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d174-f2"/> in
                    consideration of the fact that so far I have had no word from UJ though I have wired him, I am in agreement with
                    your suggestion that the “<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Quadrant</hi>” conference be started
                    about August fifteenth in the location of Montcalm.</p>
                <p>Please inform me as early as possible of exact date of meeting that will suit
                    your arrangements for transportation. If UJ moves
                    I think August seventeenth would suit me better.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d174-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d174-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d174-f2" n="2" xml:id="d174-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg393">pp. 393</ref>, <ref
